{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfppDsvjxXAjdMQb4dfYm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done — all three tests pass.\n\n- `src/str.js:11` — `reverse(s)` returns the string reversed, exported alongside `trim` and `capitalize`.\n- `test/str.test.js:18` — covers multi-char, single-char, empty, and an emoji case.\n\nOne implementation note: I used `[...s]` rather than the usual `s.split('')`. Spread iterates code points, so `reverse('ab🙂')` gives `'🙂ba'`; `split('')` iterates UTF-16 units and would split the emoji's surrogate pair, producing two orphaned halves and a mojibake character. Same cost, strictly fewer ways to be wrong — the emoji assertion in the test locks that in.\n\nIt still doesn't handle grapheme clusters: a combining mark (`'e\\u0301'`, rendered `é`) detaches from its base letter and reattaches to whatever lands next. Correct handling needs `Intl.Segmenter`, which is a different shape of function than the rest of this module. Worth adding only if you expect that input — say so and I'll do it.\n\nConsistent with the other two helpers, `reverse(null)` throws. No commits made."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":258,"cache_read_input_tokens":22454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":258,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"223d25bc-14b0-421a-b45c-061d9d6c6af3","uuid":"5a03103c-ad50-4e5e-bb73-e50ea3116180","timestamp":"2026-10-08T13:02:42.098Z","request_id":"req_011CfppDsh6K9WrmuHFmCV3w"}
